1
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:16,249
( DISTANT HAMMERING )

2
00:00:34,051 --> 00:00:35,568
( WOMAN SCREAMING )

3
00:00:35,635 --> 00:00:38,904
MINISTER : " ... things I heard , as it were ,

4
00:00:38,972 --> 00:00:41,908
" the voice of much people in heaven , saying ,

5
00:00:41,975 --> 00:00:43,443
" Hallelujah .

6
00:00:43,510 --> 00:00:48,665
" Salvation and glory and power is to our God .

7
00:00:48,732 --> 00:00:52,318
" For true and just are his judgments ,

8
00:00:52,386 --> 00:00:55,204
" who hath judged the great harlot which corrupted ...

9
00:00:58,859 --> 00:01:00,760
" ... with her fornication ,

10
00:01:00,827 --> 00:01:06,416
" and hath revenged the blood of his servants , at her hands .

11
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:11,421
" Come , gather yourselves together to the great supper of God .

12
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:16,775
" That you may eat the flesh of kings , and the flesh of tribunes ,

13
00:01:16,843 --> 00:01:21,547
" and the flesh of mighty men , and the flesh of horses ,

14
00:01:21,615 --> 00:01:24,917
" and of them that sit on them ,

15
00:01:24,985 --> 00:01:28,221
" and the flesh of all freemen and bondmen ,

16
00:01:28,288 --> 00:01:31,591
" and of little and of great .

17
00:01:31,658 --> 00:01:36,028
" And I saw the beast , and the kings of the earth ,

18
00:01:36,096 --> 00:01:40,766
" and their armies gathered together to make war with him

19
00:01:40,834 --> 00:01:43,202
" that sat upon the horse ... "

20
00:01:43,270 --> 00:01:45,521
Bring on some water !

21
00:01:45,589 --> 00:01:50,710
" And the beast was taken , and with him the false prophet ,

22
00:01:50,778 --> 00:01:53,095
" who wrought signs before him ,

23
00:01:53,163 --> 00:01:57,851
" wherewith he seduced them who received the character of the beast ,

24
00:01:57,918 --> 00:01:59,919
" and who adored his image .

25
00:01:59,987 --> 00:02:06,609
" These two were cast alive into the pool of fire , burning with brimstone .

26
00:02:06,677 --> 00:02:09,195
" And the rest were slain by the sword

27
00:02:09,263 --> 00:02:11,697
" of him that sitteth upon the horse ...

28
00:02:11,765 --> 00:02:15,468
" ... and all the birds were filled with their flesh . "

29
00:04:39,062 --> 00:04:41,330
MALE NARRATOR : The year is 1645 .

30
00:04:41,397 --> 00:04:44,233
England is in the grip of bloody civil war .

31
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:47,103
On the one side stand the Royalist party of King Charles ,

32
00:04:47,170 --> 00:04:50,840
on the other , Cromwell 's Parliamentary party , the Roundheads .

33
00:04:50,907 --> 00:04:53,575
The structure of law and order has collapsed .

34
00:04:53,643 --> 00:04:56,879
Local magistrates indulge their individual whims ,

35
00:04:56,947 --> 00:04:58,914
justice and injustice are dispensed

36
00:04:58,982 --> 00:05:00,916
in more or less equal quantities

37
00:05:00,984 --> 00:05:02,585
and without opposition ,

38
00:05:02,652 --> 00:05:05,888
an atmosphere in which the unscrupulous revel

39
00:05:05,956 --> 00:05:07,723
and the likes of Matthew Hopkins

40
00:05:07,791 --> 00:05:10,093
take full advantage of the situation .

41
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:12,495
In a time where the superstitions of country folk

42
00:05:12,563 --> 00:05:13,963
are still a powerful factor ,

43
00:05:14,030 --> 00:05:15,898
Hopkins preys upon them ,

44
00:05:15,966 --> 00:05:18,234
torturing and killing in a supposed drive

45
00:05:18,302 --> 00:05:20,503
to eliminate witchcraft from the country

46
00:05:20,571 --> 00:05:23,973
and doing so with the full blessingof what law there is .

47
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:26,442
However , his influence is confined largely

48
00:05:26,510 --> 00:05:28,377
to the eastern sector of the country ,

49
00:05:28,445 --> 00:05:32,615
East Anglia , which is held firmly in Cromwell 's grasp ,

50
00:05:32,682 --> 00:05:35,218
but not so firmly that the Roundhead cavalry patrols

51
00:05:35,285 --> 00:05:36,936
have everything their own way ,

52
00:05:37,004 --> 00:05:39,305
for there still exists an ever-present threat

53
00:05:39,373 --> 00:05:41,640
from the remnants of the Royalist armies ,

54
00:05:41,708 --> 00:05:45,011
desperately foraging for food , horses and supplies .

55
00:05:48,015 --> 00:05:49,415
Stop that , Richard .

56
00:05:49,482 --> 00:05:50,850
What ?

57
00:05:50,918 --> 00:05:52,351
What you 're thinking .

58
00:05:52,419 --> 00:05:53,786
What am I thinking ?

59
00:05:53,854 --> 00:05:56,622
Ungodly thoughts of your Sara , that 's my guess .

60
00:05:56,690 --> 00:05:59,058
Thoughts of Sara , yes . Ungodly ?

61
00:05:59,125 --> 00:06:01,594
Depends on how you look at it .

62
00:06:01,662 --> 00:06:03,379
And you , a supporter of Cromwell ...

63
00:06:03,447 --> 00:06:05,264
Hold your talking , you two .

64
00:06:05,331 --> 00:06:07,133
Yes , sir . Of course , sir .

65
00:06:08,869 --> 00:06:12,388
We 'll be stopping in a few minutes to give the horses a rest .

66
00:06:12,456 --> 00:06:14,690
You can gabble all you want then .

67
00:06:28,889 --> 00:06:31,857
15 minutes and we 'll be on our way again .

68
00:06:38,982 --> 00:06:40,449
( SCREAMS )

69
00:06:40,517 --> 00:06:43,736
Get down . Royalist snipers .

70
00:06:43,804 --> 00:06:46,772
Probably only a few of them after food and horses .

71
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:49,308
We 'll flush the bastards out in no time .

72
00:06:49,375 --> 00:06:52,478
Marshall , you stop behind to keep an eye on the nags .

73
00:06:52,546 --> 00:06:55,581
The rest of you follow me and keep spread out .

74
00:07:52,038 --> 00:07:54,073
SOLDIER : Captain , look ! There 's one !

75
00:07:54,141 --> 00:07:55,925
CAPTAIN : I see him ! Follow !

76
00:07:57,694 --> 00:07:58,694
( GUN FIRES )

77
00:07:58,762 --> 00:08:00,562
( MAN SCREAMING )

78
00:08:00,630 --> 00:08:02,231
CAPTAIN : Harcourt , this way .

79
00:08:03,833 --> 00:08:05,367
( MAN SCREAMING )

80
00:08:34,981 --> 00:08:36,548
Robert ?

81
00:08:43,723 --> 00:08:45,057
Captain ?

82
00:08:48,761 --> 00:08:51,163
Captain Gordon , is that you ?

83
00:08:51,231 --> 00:08:53,231
We 're here , trooper Marshall .

84
00:08:54,067 --> 00:08:55,868
It 's quite all right .

85
00:08:57,070 --> 00:08:58,303
Getting a bit nervous , were you , lad ?

86
00:08:58,371 --> 00:08:59,638
Aye , just a bit , sir .

87
00:08:59,706 --> 00:09:01,640
Well , no need to worry . We got them all , I reckon ...

88
00:09:01,708 --> 00:09:03,709
Not quite all . One of them got away , sir ,

89
00:09:03,777 --> 00:09:05,711
though I put my sword in him first .

90
00:09:05,779 --> 00:09:07,412
We 'd better move on out of this wood , then .

91
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:09,664
If he has got away , he could still be dangerous .

92
00:09:09,732 --> 00:09:12,051
Swallow , bury Brace 's body as soon as you can .

93
00:09:12,119 --> 00:09:13,085
Look out , sir !

94
00:09:13,153 --> 00:09:14,303
( SCREAMS )

95
00:09:20,827 --> 00:09:22,444
Thank you , trooper Marshall .

96
00:09:22,512 --> 00:09:24,079
He was trying to kill you , sir .

97
00:09:24,146 --> 00:09:25,781
I gather that , trooper .

98
00:09:25,849 --> 00:09:27,649
It was a lucky shot , sir .

99
00:09:27,967 --> 00:09:29,401
Yes .

100
00:09:29,469 --> 00:09:31,870
Nevertheless , it could have ended my career for good .

101
00:09:31,971 --> 00:09:33,338
Right , we move out .

102
00:09:33,406 --> 00:09:36,492
Swallow , join us as soon as you 've finished your business here .

103
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:37,809
Harcourt , give him a hand to remove the bodies .

104
00:09:37,877 --> 00:09:39,144
Yes , sir .

105
00:09:50,389 --> 00:09:53,225
ROBERT : So , you granted young Richard here leave , did you , Captain ?

106
00:09:53,292 --> 00:09:54,426
I did .

107
00:09:54,494 --> 00:09:55,828
Aye , two days .

108
00:09:55,895 --> 00:09:57,763
Then you 'll be away to see your girl , I suppose .

109
00:09:57,831 --> 00:09:59,164
And how will she greet you ?

110
00:09:59,232 --> 00:10:01,700
Just promoted cornet for killing King 's men .

111
00:10:01,768 --> 00:10:03,201
She knows my reasons for fighting

112
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:04,637
and it 's only while the trouble lasts .

113
00:10:04,704 --> 00:10:06,171
( ROBERT CHUCKLING ) What are you laughing at ?

114
00:10:06,239 --> 00:10:07,439
Leave him be , Robert .

115
00:10:07,507 --> 00:10:08,641
Can 't you see he 's in love ?

116
00:10:08,708 --> 00:10:10,643
Aye , I 'm not ashamed of it , either .

117
00:10:10,710 --> 00:10:14,013
A toast , lads , to the lovely women of Suffolk .

118
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:15,714
And may they keep their beds warm

119
00:10:15,782 --> 00:10:17,816
for General Cromwell 's gallant men .

120
00:10:17,884 --> 00:10:19,351
( SOLDIERS LAUGHING )

121
00:10:39,322 --> 00:10:41,323
Come on , boy . Nearly home .

122
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:34,009
Well !

123
00:11:34,994 --> 00:11:37,295
Master Marshall , welcome .

124
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:38,830
I trust you 're well , sir .

125
00:11:38,899 --> 00:11:41,367
My body is as strong as ever ,

126
00:11:42,769 --> 00:11:44,169
but the war continues ?

127
00:11:44,237 --> 00:11:46,405
Aye , we still fight . And why ...

128
00:11:46,407 --> 00:11:47,706
Well , my company 's recruiting .

129
00:11:47,773 --> 00:11:49,307
I have two days ' leave .

130
00:11:49,375 --> 00:11:51,610
Then you must eat with us this evening . I thank you , sir .

131
00:11:51,678 --> 00:11:55,164
We still have good food for all you soldiers take it from us .

132
00:11:55,231 --> 00:11:57,983
And ale . Come , we shall drink together .

133
00:12:07,343 --> 00:12:08,844
After your experience ,

134
00:12:08,912 --> 00:12:10,713
it is likely our village has grown

135
00:12:10,780 --> 00:12:12,514
a little smaller for you , eh , Richard ?

136
00:12:12,582 --> 00:12:15,767
Not so much smaller as lacking in promise , perhaps .

137
00:12:17,637 --> 00:12:21,740
In Ipswich or Cambridge , a man might find better opportunities .

138
00:12:21,808 --> 00:12:24,776
Richard , if you took Sara to wife ...

139
00:12:24,844 --> 00:12:26,928
You mean , you 'd give us your blessing ?

140
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:28,697
You would take her away from here ?

141
00:12:28,765 --> 00:12:29,999
You honor me , sir ,

142
00:12:30,066 --> 00:12:31,984
but I only have a small farm that belonged to my father

143
00:12:32,051 --> 00:12:33,251
and my soldier 's pay , which is ...

144
00:12:33,319 --> 00:12:37,372
I am little concerned with your ill kept lands .

145
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:41,243
And still less for the silver you get for killing good Christians .

146
00:12:43,496 --> 00:12:47,432
Well , forgive me . That was unjust .

147
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:50,202
But there is trouble coming to this village

148
00:12:50,204 --> 00:12:52,938
and I want Sara far away before it arrives .

149
00:12:53,005 --> 00:12:56,842
Surely Suffolk should be free from the King 's armies .

150
00:12:56,909 --> 00:13:00,712
It 's not only the King 's armies which bring death this year .

151
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:04,216
A lack of order in the land encourages strange ideas .

152
00:13:04,284 --> 00:13:06,351
You mean more rebellion ?

153
00:13:06,419 --> 00:13:08,753
I 'm sorry , you have worries enough already .

154
00:13:08,822 --> 00:13:12,291
But give me your word that you will soon take Sara away from here

155
00:13:12,359 --> 00:13:14,693
and you shall ask her consent tonight .

156
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:16,879
You have my word on that , sir .

157
00:13:16,946 --> 00:13:18,814
Good , Richard . Good .

158
00:13:23,669 --> 00:13:25,270
That 's right , my dear .

159
00:13:25,337 --> 00:13:27,022
Master Richard Marshall .

160
00:13:27,089 --> 00:13:28,874
Farm boy into soldier .

161
00:13:28,942 --> 00:13:31,493
Welcome back , Master Marshall .

162
00:13:31,561 --> 00:13:34,046
I 'm glad to be back , Mistress Sara .

163
00:13:34,113 --> 00:13:38,483
By the way , Sara , I expect the meal at the usual time .

164
00:13:38,551 --> 00:13:40,185
( CHUCKLING ) Yes , Uncle .

165
00:13:41,737 --> 00:13:44,389
Your uncle has agreed to our marriage .

166
00:13:47,259 --> 00:13:48,493
Richard .

167
00:13:48,561 --> 00:13:50,229
( RICHARD LAUGHING )

168
00:13:56,135 --> 00:14:00,005
Oh , the army has taught you rough manners .

169
00:14:12,252 --> 00:14:14,319
Sara , why is he frightened ?

170
00:14:16,489 --> 00:14:18,423
There have been threats to us since you were last here .

171
00:14:18,491 --> 00:14:19,824
Threats ? Why ?

172
00:14:19,893 --> 00:14:21,159
We 've been called papists and idolaters ,

173
00:14:21,227 --> 00:14:23,661
and filth chalked up on the walls .

174
00:14:23,729 --> 00:14:25,264
They say we 're King 's creatures

175
00:14:25,331 --> 00:14:26,831
and should be pilloried and worse .

176
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:28,000
Who says these things ?

177
00:14:28,067 --> 00:14:30,835
We 've become outcasts in our own village .

178
00:14:34,573 --> 00:14:36,008
Rest easy .

179
00:14:37,676 --> 00:14:39,744
Now , no one shall harm you .

180
00:14:40,446 --> 00:14:42,347
I put my oath to that .

181
00:14:48,922 --> 00:14:50,789
Have you arranged a day for the wedding , Richard ?

182
00:14:50,856 --> 00:14:51,990
No , sir .

183
00:14:52,058 --> 00:14:54,359
Much depends on how the armies move .

184
00:14:54,427 --> 00:14:56,328
Remember , it must be soon .

185
00:14:56,396 --> 00:14:59,431
But how certain are your fears of this danger ?

186
00:15:00,533 --> 00:15:03,568
Perhaps just an old man 's bad dream ,

187
00:15:03,636 --> 00:15:06,621
and being an old man , I must early to my bed .

188
00:15:06,689 --> 00:15:07,689
Good night , my dear .

189
00:15:07,757 --> 00:15:09,324
Good night , Uncle .

190
00:15:09,392 --> 00:15:12,895
Oh , and Sara , remember to seethe doors are well bolted .

191
00:15:12,962 --> 00:15:14,296
Yes , Uncle .

192
00:15:14,364 --> 00:15:18,100
And Richard , don 't keep Mistress Sara up too late .

193
00:15:18,167 --> 00:15:20,568
Country women need full eight hours in their beds

194
00:15:20,636 --> 00:15:23,405
if they 're to be proper wives and mothers .

195
00:15:24,374 --> 00:15:25,740
Goodnight , Cornet .

196
00:15:25,808 --> 00:15:27,109
Goodnight , sir .

197
00:15:35,218 --> 00:15:38,987
And will you make a proper wife and mother , Sara ?

198
00:15:39,055 --> 00:15:41,423
I still have much to learn , Richard .

199
00:15:41,490 --> 00:15:43,325
I 'll teach you .

200
00:15:43,392 --> 00:15:47,129
Now , didn 't your uncle just say you must early to bed ?

201
00:15:47,197 --> 00:15:48,197
He did .

202
00:15:48,264 --> 00:15:50,999
And isn 't he a wise man ? He is .

203
00:15:51,067 --> 00:15:52,167
Right .

204
00:16:57,616 --> 00:16:59,584
How much further , Matthew ?

205
00:16:59,651 --> 00:17:01,719
You will not call me Matthew .

206
00:17:01,787 --> 00:17:03,922
I 'm not one of your drinking cronies ,

207
00:17:03,990 --> 00:17:06,024
carousing and wenching in the taverns .

208
00:17:06,092 --> 00:17:07,225
Aye , you 're not that , sir .

209
00:17:07,293 --> 00:17:09,111
Remember , John Stearne , you ride with me

210
00:17:09,178 --> 00:17:10,912
only because you help me in my work .

211
00:17:10,980 --> 00:17:12,597
Oh , you call it work ?

212
00:17:12,682 --> 00:17:14,283
It 's the Lord 's work , a noble thing ...

213
00:17:14,350 --> 00:17:15,717
And a profitable one .

214
00:17:15,719 --> 00:17:18,303
The Good Lord paying in silver for every hanging .

215
00:17:18,305 --> 00:17:20,405
That is blasphemy , Stearne . Hold your tongue .

216
00:17:20,473 --> 00:17:23,408
I 'm merely an honest man who helps you get your confessions .

217
00:17:23,476 --> 00:17:26,494
The law has prescribed due methods of interrogation .

218
00:17:26,562 --> 00:17:28,730
And I have been blessed with the skills to carry them out .

219
00:17:28,798 --> 00:17:31,766
Oh , stop your gabbling . We have work to do in Brandeston .

220
00:17:31,834 --> 00:17:33,017
Who is it this time ?

221
00:17:33,085 --> 00:17:35,554
- The message tells of a priest . - A priest ?

222
00:17:35,621 --> 00:17:38,707
One who gives worship to Satan and calls him Lord .

223
00:17:38,774 --> 00:17:41,376
Oh , with the priest himself a witch ,

224
00:17:41,444 --> 00:17:44,029
there 'll be others corrupted , too , I 'm thinking .

225
00:17:44,097 --> 00:17:46,431
You enjoy torture , don 't you , Stearne ?

226
00:17:46,498 --> 00:17:49,818
And you , sir ?

227
00:17:53,439 --> 00:17:55,023
Goodbye , sir .

228
00:17:55,091 --> 00:17:56,624
LOWES : God be with you , Richard .

229
00:17:58,461 --> 00:18:00,645
Goodbye , Richard . Goodbye , Sara .

230
00:18:01,514 --> 00:18:03,181
I 'll see you again soon .

231
00:18:14,660 --> 00:18:15,827
( BELL CHIMING )

232
00:18:46,825 --> 00:18:49,327
Given up ale for star-gazing , Tom Salter ?

233
00:18:49,395 --> 00:18:52,631
Not star-gazing , Master Marshall . Waiting .

234
00:18:52,698 --> 00:18:54,332
What for ?

235
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:56,701
Matthew Hopkins , a lawyer .

236
00:18:56,768 --> 00:19:00,038
Must be important , that you wait after dark .

237
00:19:00,106 --> 00:19:01,439
It is , that .

238
00:19:01,507 --> 00:19:02,807
Aye .

239
00:19:02,875 --> 00:19:06,511
Well , if I see a lawyer on the road , I 'll tell him you 're here .

240
00:19:38,411 --> 00:19:40,529
How far is it to Brandeston , friend ?

241
00:19:40,596 --> 00:19:42,297
- About three miles . - Thank you .

242
00:19:42,365 --> 00:19:44,199
- Are you the lawyer ? - Aye .

243
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:46,234
- Name of Hopkins ? - Aye , Matthew Hopkins .

244
00:19:46,302 --> 00:19:48,102
And this is my assistant , John Stearne .

245
00:19:48,170 --> 00:19:49,921
Why do you want to know , soldier ?

246
00:19:49,973 --> 00:19:51,906
There 's some men from the village back there , waiting for you .

247
00:19:51,975 --> 00:19:53,608
Aye , they sent for us .

248
00:19:53,676 --> 00:19:56,278
What would a lawyer want in Brandeston ?

249
00:19:56,346 --> 00:20:00,798
A man who may not be what he seems to be . Come Stearne .

250
00:20:18,134 --> 00:20:19,651
- John Lowes is his name . - An evil man .

251
00:20:19,719 --> 00:20:21,686
- A papist . - Yeah , burning candles and all .

252
00:20:21,753 --> 00:20:24,272
That is no proof of witchcraft in itself .

253
00:20:24,340 --> 00:20:26,407
Dressed himself in devil 's garments , he did .

254
00:20:26,475 --> 00:20:28,560
- And made unholy signs . - Yeah , he did . I saw him .

255
00:20:28,627 --> 00:20:30,295
I will find out the truth for you .

256
00:20:30,363 --> 00:20:31,964
Have no fear , friends .

257
00:20:49,215 --> 00:20:50,815
( KNOCKING ON DOOR )

258
00:20:55,671 --> 00:20:56,771
Yes ?

259
00:20:58,974 --> 00:21:00,375
John Lowes ?

260
00:21:18,861 --> 00:21:20,228
So , it has come to this .

261
00:21:20,296 --> 00:21:23,131
You accuse me , a priest , of working with the Devil .

262
00:21:23,198 --> 00:21:24,933
We can only judge by the evidence .

263
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,101
And there 's a lot of that , old man .

264
00:21:27,169 --> 00:21:29,304
I reject your accusations totally .

265
00:21:29,371 --> 00:21:30,488
He 's going to give us trouble .

266
00:21:30,556 --> 00:21:33,025
A simple confession , priest , that 's all we ask .

267
00:21:33,092 --> 00:21:34,242
Help us .

268
00:21:34,310 --> 00:21:36,778
We 've got a lot of work to do in Brandeston .

269
00:21:36,846 --> 00:21:38,813
Leave my house , the pair of you .

270
00:21:38,880 --> 00:21:40,482
I told you he was going to be difficult .

271
00:21:40,549 --> 00:21:43,418
I reject your foul suggestions ! Leave here at once !

272
00:21:43,486 --> 00:21:46,053
All you reject is the true God !

273
00:21:46,122 --> 00:21:47,422
Take him , Stearne .

274
00:21:47,490 --> 00:21:49,390
Look for the Devil 's marks upon him .

275
00:21:49,458 --> 00:21:51,442
Right . Help us , you two .

276
00:22:00,619 --> 00:22:03,138
( MUMBLING IN LATIN )

277
00:22:03,206 --> 00:22:04,706
Look , he still prays to Satan .

278
00:22:04,773 --> 00:22:07,008
Get on with your task .

279
00:22:07,075 --> 00:22:08,910
If the Devil made you a priest ,

280
00:22:08,978 --> 00:22:11,446
he 's going to have hidden his mark with a lot of care .

281
00:22:14,116 --> 00:22:15,283
( SCREAMING )

282
00:22:19,122 --> 00:22:20,438
To what purpose is this ?

283
00:22:20,506 --> 00:22:22,106
When the Devil buys a soul ,

284
00:22:22,174 --> 00:22:25,326
he marks the person 's flesh , so we will know him .

285
00:22:25,394 --> 00:22:29,497
If such a mark is pricked , no blood will flow , nor pain be felt .

286
00:22:30,449 --> 00:22:31,282
( SCREAMING )

287
00:22:35,688 --> 00:22:37,655
Mistress Sara ? Mistress Sara ?

288
00:22:37,723 --> 00:22:39,423
They 've come for him .

289
00:22:39,491 --> 00:22:41,126
( BOTH CHATTERING )

290
00:23:10,139 --> 00:23:12,257
Seems Satan has hidden his mark well , Matthew .

291
00:23:12,325 --> 00:23:13,625
Set him to running .

292
00:23:13,692 --> 00:23:15,359
Quick , then , you two , around the table .

293
00:23:15,427 --> 00:23:17,245
And keep him moving .

294
00:23:37,116 --> 00:23:38,983
You would be his niece .

295
00:23:40,085 --> 00:23:41,452
Your name , child ?

296
00:23:41,520 --> 00:23:42,553
Sara .

297
00:23:42,621 --> 00:23:46,006
I am Matthew Hopkins , Witchfinder .

298
00:23:46,074 --> 00:23:50,044
Being his niece , you , too , may be corrupted by Satan .

299
00:23:50,979 --> 00:23:53,414
No , not his niece .

300
00:23:54,216 --> 00:23:55,617
A foundling ,

301
00:23:55,684 --> 00:23:57,318
taken in by him and his housekeeper .

302
00:23:57,386 --> 00:23:59,604
- Are you telling me the truth , child ? - Yes , yes , of course .

303
00:23:59,671 --> 00:24:01,840
When she died , I became his servant .

304
00:24:01,907 --> 00:24:04,159
And you 've remained innocent all of these years ?

305
00:24:04,226 --> 00:24:05,160
Yes , sir , entirely .

306
00:24:05,227 --> 00:24:06,961
I trust you know the old man ?

307
00:24:07,029 --> 00:24:08,229
Better than anyone .

308
00:24:08,297 --> 00:24:12,149
In private talk , we may shed some light on his innocence .

309
00:24:12,901 --> 00:24:14,152
Private ?

310
00:24:14,219 --> 00:24:16,821
Yes , away from the distraction of the crowd .

311
00:24:16,889 --> 00:24:18,723
Perhaps in the quiet of your room tonight ,

312
00:24:18,790 --> 00:24:22,093
you might be able to help me prove him guiltless .

313
00:24:22,160 --> 00:24:25,396
Would you release him now ?

314
00:24:25,464 --> 00:24:28,900
You might be convinced tonight that this is all needless .

315
00:24:34,540 --> 00:24:38,726
And you will make every effort to present the facts to me ?

316
00:24:38,794 --> 00:24:40,728
You may come to my room tonight , sir .

317
00:24:40,796 --> 00:24:42,179
At what hour ?

318
00:24:43,633 --> 00:24:48,403
At 8 : 00 , if you 'll release him now .

319
00:24:50,072 --> 00:24:55,243
All right . He can sleep in the jail , and we 'll be rid of him .

320
00:25:10,025 --> 00:25:13,461
SALTER : Come on ! Get up , you papist bastard !

321
00:25:16,866 --> 00:25:18,366
Has he confessed yet ?

322
00:25:18,434 --> 00:25:19,801
Not a word .

323
00:25:19,869 --> 00:25:21,202
Well , then stop this .

324
00:25:21,270 --> 00:25:22,904
But he hasn 't confessed .

325
00:25:22,971 --> 00:25:26,808
Take him to the jail . We 'll continue the interrogation tomorrow .

326
00:25:26,876 --> 00:25:29,010
LOWES : Jail ...

327
00:25:29,078 --> 00:25:30,745
You heard what he said .

328
00:25:33,048 --> 00:25:34,399
Quiet down , you animal .

329
00:25:34,467 --> 00:25:35,967
( WOMAN GIGGLING )

330
00:25:36,034 --> 00:25:38,669
You know what , Marston ? There were these couple of right filthy girls ,

331
00:25:38,737 --> 00:25:39,904
filthy they were !

332
00:25:39,972 --> 00:25:41,072
Horrible to behold , horrible !

333
00:25:41,140 --> 00:25:42,273
- Witches ? - Yes , both of them .

334
00:25:42,341 --> 00:25:44,175
We hanged them , Matthew and me .

335
00:25:44,243 --> 00:25:46,344
Matthew . You know Matthew , he 's my partner .

336
00:25:46,412 --> 00:25:48,546
Did it take you long to get a confession out of them , John ?

337
00:25:48,614 --> 00:25:50,548
Well , a couple of days with one of them , the other one ...

338
00:25:50,616 --> 00:25:52,366
Do you want more ale , sir ?

339
00:25:55,270 --> 00:25:58,105
SALTER : Go on , then ? Come on . What about the other one ? Tell us about her .

340
00:25:58,173 --> 00:25:59,273
STEARNE : Oh , yeah , the other one .

341
00:25:59,341 --> 00:26:01,208
Now , she was a real strange one , she was .

342
00:26:01,276 --> 00:26:04,245
Loved us for it , like she wanted to get strung up .

343
00:26:04,312 --> 00:26:06,414
Reckon that was the only bit of excitement she ever had .

344
00:26:08,250 --> 00:26:10,584
Well , go on , then , Mr. Stearne .

345
00:26:11,553 --> 00:26:13,054
Go on .

346
00:26:14,123 --> 00:26:15,856
( GIRL SCREAMING )

347
00:26:33,308 --> 00:26:36,077
HOPKINS : Sara , I 've come to question you .

348
00:26:41,550 --> 00:26:43,618
You came here for a purpose , sir .

349
00:26:43,686 --> 00:26:47,154
I came here to get your evidence about the priest .

350
00:26:48,390 --> 00:26:50,725
He 's been kind to me .

351
00:26:50,792 --> 00:26:53,528
Perhaps he had a motive .

352
00:26:53,596 --> 00:26:57,465
Men sometimes have strange motives for the things they do .

353
00:27:00,102 --> 00:27:01,603
I know .

354
00:27:01,670 --> 00:27:06,641
My motive in coming here was to find the truth .

355
00:27:19,288 --> 00:27:20,655
How about the priest , Master Hopkins ?

356
00:27:20,723 --> 00:27:22,457
We 'll have done with him in a day or two .

357
00:27:22,524 --> 00:27:24,225
Have no fear , child .

358
00:27:24,293 --> 00:27:27,128
- He 's been good to mein his way . - He is an idolater .

359
00:27:27,195 --> 00:27:29,664
He must confess and die . Stearne will see to that .

360
00:27:29,732 --> 00:27:31,899
Oh , no , please ! Don 't let him be harmed , please !

361
00:27:31,967 --> 00:27:36,604
You seek to protect a witch from rightful justice ?

362
00:27:36,672 --> 00:27:38,939
Oh , no , not that , but couldn 't he be kept in a cell ?

363
00:27:39,007 --> 00:27:41,041
He could do no harm from a prison cell . Oh , please !

364
00:27:41,109 --> 00:27:43,695
But justice must be done , my dear .

365
00:27:43,762 --> 00:27:45,296
Grant me this .

366
00:27:47,733 --> 00:27:49,400
Please , Matthew .

367
00:27:57,793 --> 00:28:00,928
HOPKINS : Past noon , you unkempt lout . Get up !

368
00:28:05,667 --> 00:28:06,667
Get away !

369
00:28:06,735 --> 00:28:08,035
( WOMAN WHIMPERING )

370
00:28:10,005 --> 00:28:11,606
I need air .

371
00:28:19,982 --> 00:28:21,616
( STEARNE RETCHING )

372
00:28:29,791 --> 00:28:30,892
Where 's the priest ?

373
00:28:30,959 --> 00:28:32,994
Where you put him , in the jail .

374
00:28:41,252 --> 00:28:44,488
We 'll get him out and start questioning him , then , eh ?

375
00:28:44,556 --> 00:28:46,157
- No . - What ?

376
00:28:46,225 --> 00:28:47,258
He stays where he is .

377
00:28:47,325 --> 00:28:48,659
But we have no confession at all .

378
00:28:48,661 --> 00:28:51,779
I said we 'll leave him in the cell .

379
00:28:51,847 --> 00:28:54,281
All right , then . All right .

380
00:28:56,351 --> 00:28:57,552
What about the women ?

381
00:28:57,619 --> 00:28:59,236
When are we going to start interrogating them ?

382
00:28:59,304 --> 00:29:01,940
I hear tell they 've a good few witches around this place .

383
00:29:02,007 --> 00:29:03,341
When you 're in fit condition .

384
00:29:03,408 --> 00:29:05,243
I 'm fighting-fit as it is .

385
00:29:06,244 --> 00:29:08,996
Oh , and where were you last night , Matthew ?

386
00:29:09,064 --> 00:29:10,464
I hear tell you 've been a-wandering .

387
00:29:10,532 --> 00:29:12,767
You hear tell too much , man .

388
00:29:36,358 --> 00:29:37,892
( WOMAN CRYING )

389
00:29:42,865 --> 00:29:45,033
You , there , old man .

390
00:29:45,100 --> 00:29:47,451
Master Hopkins , the Witchfinder ,

391
00:29:47,519 --> 00:29:51,289
he says you 're to be kept here , interrogated no further .

392
00:30:12,127 --> 00:30:13,895
Where are you off to , John ?

393
00:30:13,963 --> 00:30:15,730
I 'm going for a walk .

394
00:30:15,797 --> 00:30:16,965
By myself .

395
00:32:25,994 --> 00:32:27,995
( DOG BARKING )

396
00:32:40,308 --> 00:32:41,459
( WOMAN SCREAMING )

397
00:32:41,526 --> 00:32:44,895
STEARNE : Tell me ! Tell me ! Tell me !

398
00:32:47,399 --> 00:32:50,868
Tell me that ! Come on ! Tell me !

399
00:32:51,537 --> 00:32:53,153
Confess , witch !

400
00:32:53,221 --> 00:32:54,855
Tell us your foul iniquities !

401
00:32:54,923 --> 00:32:56,490
No !

402
00:32:56,558 --> 00:32:59,977
Your familiars , woman . Confess !

403
00:33:00,045 --> 00:33:01,762
( STEARNE LAUGHING )

404
00:33:03,865 --> 00:33:08,619
Stop . For God 's sake , stop .

405
00:33:08,687 --> 00:33:11,822
Quiet , old man , and be thankful you 're not getting the same .

406
00:33:12,824 --> 00:33:14,058
( STEARNE YELLING AT WOMAN )

407
00:33:14,125 --> 00:33:16,193
( WOMAN SCREAMING )

408
00:33:16,195 --> 00:33:19,347
How many of them ? A dog ? A ferret ?

409
00:33:19,414 --> 00:33:21,515
Come on , tell them !

410
00:33:23,752 --> 00:33:27,188
John . The Witchfinder , he 's coming .

411
00:33:27,256 --> 00:33:28,656
( WOMAN SCREAMING )

412
00:33:36,364 --> 00:33:39,783
I trust you are using the prescribed methods , Stearne ?

413
00:33:39,851 --> 00:33:41,368
Naturally .

414
00:33:42,470 --> 00:33:43,754
Has she confessed ?

415
00:33:43,821 --> 00:33:46,557
Well , give me time . She 's only been here an hour .

416
00:33:46,625 --> 00:33:48,525
Continue with the interrogation .

417
00:33:48,593 --> 00:33:50,427
I shall be gone for a while .

418
00:33:50,512 --> 00:33:55,565
You 're always going off somewhere , sir , aren 't you ?

419
00:33:55,633 --> 00:33:57,018
What do you mean ?

420
00:33:57,085 --> 00:33:59,437
Nothing .

421
00:33:59,504 --> 00:34:01,838
I 've been called over the hill to the next village .

422
00:34:01,906 --> 00:34:04,158
I shall be back by tomorrow .

423
00:34:04,226 --> 00:34:06,711
You will remain in charge here .

424
00:34:06,778 --> 00:34:09,246
Carry on your work while you 're away , aye , sir ?

425
00:34:09,314 --> 00:34:10,581
Indeed .

426
00:34:11,750 --> 00:34:12,933
And the priest ?

427
00:34:13,001 --> 00:34:14,952
I said to leave him be .

428
00:34:19,140 --> 00:34:20,541
( WOMAN CRYING )

429
00:34:26,415 --> 00:34:27,415
( SLAPPING )

430
00:34:27,482 --> 00:34:29,283
( WOMAN SCREAMING )

431
00:34:58,463 --> 00:35:00,081
What do you want ?

432
00:35:02,317 --> 00:35:03,884
You .

433
00:35:03,952 --> 00:35:05,535
Where 's Master Hopkins ?

434
00:35:06,637 --> 00:35:07,738
Gone .

435
00:35:07,805 --> 00:35:08,839
Gone ?

436
00:35:10,442 --> 00:35:11,591
Where ?

437
00:35:11,659 --> 00:35:12,759
Just gone .

438
00:35:13,528 --> 00:35:15,329
He 's left me in charge .

439
00:35:25,723 --> 00:35:28,041
( SCREAMING ) No ! No !

440
00:35:37,669 --> 00:35:39,570
No !

441
00:35:39,638 --> 00:35:43,340
And don 't think I don 't know why the old priest is being spared , eh ?

442
00:35:46,411 --> 00:35:48,412
( STEARNE GRUNTING )

443
00:35:48,480 --> 00:35:49,746
( SARA SCREAMING )

444
00:36:50,308 --> 00:36:51,775
( DOG BARKING )

445
00:37:00,469 --> 00:37:01,969
Stearne , the priest .

446
00:37:02,037 --> 00:37:03,471
I 've changed my mind .

447
00:37:18,536 --> 00:37:19,770
STEARNE : Confess !

448
00:37:20,973 --> 00:37:22,340
Confess .

449
00:37:28,463 --> 00:37:29,880
He confessed . You heard him .

450
00:37:29,948 --> 00:37:32,583
I 've heard nothing yet , Master Hopkins .

451
00:37:32,650 --> 00:37:35,987
Refresh Master Salter 's memory , Stearne .

452
00:37:41,293 --> 00:37:43,126
You heard him .

453
00:37:45,613 --> 00:37:47,331
You did , too .

454
00:37:47,399 --> 00:37:49,200
Yes , Master Hopkins .

455
00:37:50,869 --> 00:37:52,336
Witnesses .

456
00:37:55,206 --> 00:37:56,540
( MOANING )

457
00:38:03,448 --> 00:38:06,400
SALTER : Get up , you blasted witch ! Get up !

458
00:38:07,835 --> 00:38:09,403
Come on !

459
00:38:11,956 --> 00:38:12,956
( SOBBING )

460
00:38:22,216 --> 00:38:24,184
( MAN YELLING )

461
00:38:24,252 --> 00:38:26,487
( PEOPLE YELLING AND SCREAMING )

462
00:39:07,362 --> 00:39:10,347
You are , all of you , confessed idolaters .

463
00:39:10,414 --> 00:39:12,699
However , these proceedings

464
00:39:12,767 --> 00:39:16,103
shall be carried out through due process of law .

465
00:39:16,170 --> 00:39:19,473
What law demands , we shall satisfy .

466
00:39:19,541 --> 00:39:22,976
You will each be tied in a prescribed fashion ,

467
00:39:23,044 --> 00:39:24,912
and cast into the moat .

468
00:39:24,979 --> 00:39:27,380
Should you then sink , we will know

469
00:39:27,448 --> 00:39:29,766
that your confessions are false .

470
00:39:29,834 --> 00:39:34,972
If on the other hand you are seen to swim or float ,

471
00:39:35,039 --> 00:39:39,676
then your confessions of witchcraft are proven beyond a doubt

472
00:39:39,777 --> 00:39:41,745
in the sight of God .

473
00:39:41,812 --> 00:39:45,599
And you will be withdrawn from the water

474
00:39:45,667 --> 00:39:48,001
and hanged by the neck until you are dead .

475
00:39:48,069 --> 00:39:50,638
You can 't hang me . The law forbids it !

476
00:39:50,705 --> 00:39:52,706
I 'm with child .

477
00:39:52,774 --> 00:39:55,358
And who would want to make you pregnant , witch ?

478
00:39:55,426 --> 00:39:56,927
( CROWD LAUGHING )

479
00:39:58,463 --> 00:40:01,065
Quiet . Stearne , go on with your task .

480
00:40:10,541 --> 00:40:12,108
( WOMAN CRYING )

481
00:40:17,665 --> 00:40:19,833
WOMAN : Oh , God , help me !

482
00:40:21,902 --> 00:40:23,136
( WOMAN SCREAMING )

483
00:40:46,144 --> 00:40:47,361
WOMAN : No !

484
00:40:47,429 --> 00:40:48,895
No !

485
00:40:54,519 --> 00:40:55,418
No !

486
00:40:55,486 --> 00:40:56,586
LOWE : Help me ...

487
00:41:01,792 --> 00:41:04,611
Hey , look ! One of them is gone already .

488
00:41:04,679 --> 00:41:06,696
They swim .

489
00:41:06,898 --> 00:41:08,682
The mark of Satan is upon them .

490
00:41:08,750 --> 00:41:10,600
STEARNE : Give us a hand here ! Come on !

491
00:41:11,402 --> 00:41:13,186
They must hang .

492
00:41:29,136 --> 00:41:30,771
She was innocent .

493
00:41:30,838 --> 00:41:34,874
God forgive you , Matthew Hopkins .

494
00:41:37,395 --> 00:41:38,562
Jailer ,

495
00:41:40,498 --> 00:41:42,265
take them to the tree .

496
00:42:00,418 --> 00:42:03,087
The money from the magistrate , nine guineas in silver .

497
00:42:03,154 --> 00:42:05,522
Good . Now we can leave .

498
00:42:57,207 --> 00:42:59,409
- Good morning , soldier . - Good morning .

499
00:42:59,477 --> 00:43:01,344
What 'll you be after in the way of horses , then , aye ?

500
00:43:01,412 --> 00:43:03,580
A dozen or so for General Cromwell 's armies up north .

501
00:43:03,648 --> 00:43:04,948
Well , lost a few , have you ?

502
00:43:05,016 --> 00:43:07,000
Aye , at Cheriton Wood .

503
00:43:07,068 --> 00:43:08,869
That 's a pretty sorry looking bunch of old nags

504
00:43:08,936 --> 00:43:10,037
you got in there , friend .

505
00:43:10,104 --> 00:43:11,488
The best we could find .

506
00:43:11,555 --> 00:43:12,723
Then they 'll have to do .

507
00:43:12,790 --> 00:43:13,857
A dozen you say , eh ?

508
00:43:13,925 --> 00:43:15,258
Aye .

509
00:43:15,326 --> 00:43:17,327
We 'll be back in Suffolk soon

510
00:43:17,394 --> 00:43:19,413
where , thank God , they still breed strong horses .

511
00:43:19,480 --> 00:43:21,148
Oh , I doubt you 'll find much better there .

512
00:43:21,216 --> 00:43:22,815
I 'm just back from those parts .

513
00:43:22,883 --> 00:43:24,350
The mounts up there are much like these .

514
00:43:24,419 --> 00:43:26,269
Have you been through Brandeston at all , man ?

515
00:43:26,337 --> 00:43:27,470
Brandeston ? Aye .

516
00:43:27,538 --> 00:43:29,622
And a fine commotion they 're stirring up there .

517
00:43:29,690 --> 00:43:31,124
What , over you taking their horses ?

518
00:43:31,192 --> 00:43:33,826
No , nothing like that . A mass hanging .

519
00:43:33,894 --> 00:43:34,978
- Who ? - Witches , I heard .

520
00:43:35,046 --> 00:43:36,162
Two women and a priest .

521
00:43:36,230 --> 00:43:37,498
Where was the priest from , man ?

522
00:43:37,565 --> 00:43:38,932
Brandeston , I suppose .

523
00:43:38,999 --> 00:43:40,984
A brave old boy for all his white hairs .

524
00:43:41,051 --> 00:43:42,853
Was he a friend of yours ?

525
00:43:42,920 --> 00:43:45,439
Two troopers , Gifford and Harcourt , will be here directly .

526
00:43:45,506 --> 00:43:47,057
Have them take these horses here back to the regiment

527
00:43:47,125 --> 00:43:48,125
and report that I 'm delayed .

528
00:43:48,192 --> 00:43:49,926
I 'll join them further north . Do you understand ?

529
00:43:49,994 --> 00:43:51,594
Yes , but where will you be going to ?

530
00:43:51,663 --> 00:43:53,196
Anything else ?

531
00:44:04,509 --> 00:44:05,775
( URGING HORSE )

532
00:44:30,702 --> 00:44:31,802
Sara !

533
00:44:37,759 --> 00:44:38,859
Sara ?

534
00:44:41,328 --> 00:44:42,462
Sara !

535
00:44:53,508 --> 00:44:54,758
Sara .

536
00:44:56,060 --> 00:44:57,327
Sara !

537
00:44:58,079 --> 00:44:59,179
Sara !

538
00:45:02,299 --> 00:45:03,600
Sara !

539
00:45:49,497 --> 00:45:53,166
They took him and killed him . They said he was an idolater .

540
00:45:53,234 --> 00:45:54,834
I know , I heard .

541
00:45:56,170 --> 00:45:58,171
Sara ...

542
00:45:58,239 --> 00:46:00,207
One of them , the Witchfinder ,

543
00:46:01,943 --> 00:46:03,243
he ...

544
00:46:05,179 --> 00:46:06,380
He ...

545
00:46:09,650 --> 00:46:11,418
I didn 't want to ...

546
00:46:13,754 --> 00:46:15,889
I thought I could save him .

547
00:46:18,659 --> 00:46:20,760
I thought they 'd have pity .

548
00:46:57,782 --> 00:47:01,885
We kneel before thee , oh , Lord , in humility

549
00:47:02,853 --> 00:47:05,521
to ask for a blessing on our union .

550
00:47:06,791 --> 00:47:10,727
We ask for forgiveness of our sins

551
00:47:10,795 --> 00:47:16,900
and strength to lead righteous lives as man and wife .

552
00:47:20,004 --> 00:47:25,274
We pray also for the soul of thy servant , John Lowes .

553
00:47:26,911 --> 00:47:29,045
May he know eternal peace .

554
00:47:36,170 --> 00:47:41,908
And it is in thy sight , oh , Lord , that I hereby swear

555
00:47:41,976 --> 00:47:46,113
I shall not rest from the pursuit of his murderers

556
00:47:46,180 --> 00:47:51,685
till they stand before thee , ready to answer to thee for their sins .

557
00:48:08,102 --> 00:48:10,737
Take this money and whatever you need from the rectory and go to Lavenham .

558
00:48:10,805 --> 00:48:12,622
- You 'll be safer there . - I will , Richard .

559
00:48:12,624 --> 00:48:14,658
Find lodgings and stay there .

560
00:48:14,725 --> 00:48:16,008
I 'll come to you .

561
00:48:31,108 --> 00:48:33,109
I love you very much .

562
00:48:34,812 --> 00:48:36,362
Oh , Richard !

563
00:48:56,317 --> 00:48:57,818
( SOOTHING HORSE )

564
00:50:11,041 --> 00:50:12,641
( SHEEP BLEATING )

565
00:50:23,921 --> 00:50:26,072
Shepherd , I seek two men . Witchfinders , they call themselves .

566
00:50:26,140 --> 00:50:27,173
They were said to be headed this way .

567
00:50:27,241 --> 00:50:29,742
- Matthew Hopkins and his assistant ? - Aye .

568
00:50:29,810 --> 00:50:31,895
I 've heard they 're in Hoxne ,

569
00:50:31,962 --> 00:50:35,265
about four miles yonder , but I can 't be sure .

570
00:50:35,332 --> 00:50:36,866
Thank you , Shepherd .

571
00:50:37,101 --> 00:50:38,351
SHEPHERD : Get out !

572
00:50:38,418 --> 00:50:40,019
( URGING HORSE )

573
00:51:14,488 --> 00:51:16,690
Oh , come on , Johnny , give us a kiss .

574
00:51:16,757 --> 00:51:19,025
Oh , get away from me .

575
00:51:19,093 --> 00:51:21,328
Stop it , you dirty rascal !

576
00:51:21,395 --> 00:51:23,330
Stop it !

577
00:51:23,397 --> 00:51:25,265
STEARNE : Here , I 'll bet you two pennies .

578
00:51:27,635 --> 00:51:29,368
Ale , soldier ?

579
00:51:29,436 --> 00:51:31,137
Aye , to wash the dust from my throat .

580
00:51:34,942 --> 00:51:37,076
- Another one for you ? - Aye , get a move on with it .

581
00:51:37,144 --> 00:51:38,611
She 's got a powerful thirst still .

582
00:51:38,679 --> 00:51:41,014
Landlord , I 'm looking for a man called Hopkins .

583
00:51:41,081 --> 00:51:42,148
I heard he was coming this way .

584
00:51:42,215 --> 00:51:43,449
Matthew Hopkins ?

585
00:51:43,517 --> 00:51:44,851
Would you know where he is , friend ?

586
00:51:44,919 --> 00:51:47,319
Aye , he 's gone to Cambridge today .

587
00:51:47,387 --> 00:51:48,855
But you got an accusation to make ,

588
00:51:48,923 --> 00:51:50,322
I 'll get your confession for you .

589
00:51:50,390 --> 00:51:53,059
I do the pricking , you know , not Matthew .

590
00:51:53,126 --> 00:51:54,393
I 'm your man , friend .

591
00:51:54,461 --> 00:51:55,962
John Stearne , they call me .

592
00:51:57,497 --> 00:51:58,381
( SCREAMING )

593
00:51:58,599 --> 00:52:00,633
I 'm husband to Sara Lowes .

594
00:52:02,353 --> 00:52:03,903
( WOMAN SCREAMING )

595
00:52:07,591 --> 00:52:09,091
( BOTH GRUNTING )

596
00:52:41,541 --> 00:52:43,292
- You all right , friend ? - Yeah .

597
00:52:43,360 --> 00:52:46,479
- You better get out of here . - Yeah , I 'm going , don 't worry .

598
00:52:57,841 --> 00:53:00,576
As for you , soldier , you are coming down to see the magistrate .

599
00:53:00,644 --> 00:53:03,346
Am I ? Not with you .

600
00:53:17,511 --> 00:53:19,095
( URGING HORSE )

601
00:54:55,091 --> 00:54:56,626
Quick , Matthew !

602
00:55:12,209 --> 00:55:14,393
For God 's sake , Stearne , what have you done ? Who was that ?

603
00:55:14,461 --> 00:55:16,162
- Richard Marshall . - Who ?

604
00:55:16,230 --> 00:55:18,531
He 's married to the girl , Sara .

605
00:55:18,599 --> 00:55:19,965
How did he find you ?

606
00:55:20,033 --> 00:55:21,334
He was looking for you .

607
00:55:21,401 --> 00:55:22,602
He found out about Brandeston .

608
00:55:22,669 --> 00:55:23,836
We 're going to have to separate .

609
00:55:23,903 --> 00:55:25,004
I won 't run from him .

610
00:55:25,071 --> 00:55:27,240
We have work to do down south in Lavenham .

611
00:55:27,307 --> 00:55:29,208
Not me . He 's after our blood .

612
00:55:29,276 --> 00:55:31,877
Seems to me he 's already had some of yours .

613
00:55:31,945 --> 00:55:33,846
Well , he 's not going to have any more , you understand ?

614
00:55:33,913 --> 00:55:35,214
You 're forgetting our powers .

615
00:55:35,282 --> 00:55:36,482
He could be a witch .

616
00:55:36,550 --> 00:55:38,851
He 's a man who 's out to kill both of us .

617
00:55:38,918 --> 00:55:43,722
Then it appears to me that we should take steps to see to his death first .

618
00:55:43,790 --> 00:55:45,924
Come . We travel to Lavenham .

619
00:56:14,938 --> 00:56:17,640
I full well understand your feelings , Cornet ,

620
00:56:17,708 --> 00:56:20,176
but you 're an officer of the army , a soldier ,

621
00:56:20,244 --> 00:56:22,678
and desertion is punishable by death .

622
00:56:22,746 --> 00:56:24,830
However , in this case , there are two factors

623
00:56:24,898 --> 00:56:29,134
which will stay me from subjecting you to a full court-martial .

624
00:56:29,203 --> 00:56:32,071
One , we are grouped here at Naseby

625
00:56:32,138 --> 00:56:35,074
in preparation for a major assault on the Royalist armies .

626
00:56:35,141 --> 00:56:37,476
We need every man we can get .

627
00:56:37,544 --> 00:56:40,580
And you 're a pretty good soldier , most of the time .

628
00:56:40,648 --> 00:56:42,665
Thank you , sir .

629
00:56:42,732 --> 00:56:46,585
Secondly , I would sleep ill if I had to send to the gallows

630
00:56:46,653 --> 00:56:48,570
a man who had saved my life .

631
00:56:48,638 --> 00:56:51,490
But , Cornet , remember this .

632
00:56:51,558 --> 00:56:55,194
If you should leave your command again ,

633
00:56:55,262 --> 00:56:59,832
I will have no alternative but to throw the whole weight of military law against you .

634
00:56:59,900 --> 00:57:01,100
Understand ?

635
00:57:01,168 --> 00:57:02,135
Yes , sir .

636
00:57:02,969 --> 00:57:04,687
Dismissed , Cornet .

637
00:57:09,777 --> 00:57:13,145
And may God help you in your search , Cornet Marshall .

638
00:57:31,331 --> 00:57:32,631
Robert , hello .

639
00:57:32,699 --> 00:57:34,434
- Richard , you 're back . - Aye .

640
00:57:34,501 --> 00:57:35,885
What happened with the Captain ?

641
00:57:35,953 --> 00:57:37,237
Nothing .

642
00:57:38,472 --> 00:57:41,006
I heard about Brandeston , Richard .

643
00:57:41,074 --> 00:57:42,791
Hopkins and Stearne .

644
00:57:42,859 --> 00:57:44,627
I 'll find them somewhere .

645
00:57:44,694 --> 00:57:46,095
But what can you do ?

646
00:57:46,163 --> 00:57:48,431
What proof have you that they committed any crime ?

647
00:57:48,499 --> 00:57:50,066
I 've got Sara 's word on it .

648
00:57:50,134 --> 00:57:51,817
Is that enough for the magistrates ?

649
00:57:51,885 --> 00:57:53,619
There 'll be no magistrates involved .

650
00:57:53,687 --> 00:57:55,321
What do you mean ?

651
00:58:00,610 --> 00:58:02,010
We 'll talk more later , Richard .

652
00:58:02,078 --> 00:58:03,546
We must be on our way .

653
00:58:03,613 --> 00:58:05,948
We 're after horses for this skirmish that 's coming up .

654
00:58:06,015 --> 00:58:07,049
All right .

655
00:58:07,116 --> 00:58:09,117
Hup . Come on . Hup .

656
00:58:23,216 --> 00:58:27,169
Parliament men , comrades of friend Marshall .

657
00:58:27,237 --> 00:58:29,688
There 's some good ones coming now , look .

658
00:58:29,756 --> 00:58:31,207
Hey !

659
00:58:31,275 --> 00:58:32,285
Let 's make a run for it , shall we , while we can .

660
00:58:32,285 --> 00:58:34,871
- Be calm - Yeah , but if they find out who we are ,

661
00:58:34,871 --> 00:58:36,845
- they 'll ... - They won 't . Come on .

662
00:58:50,861 --> 00:58:52,795
That 's a fine horse you 've got there , friend .

663
00:58:52,863 --> 00:58:54,864
ROBERT : The army needs mounts of such caliber .

664
00:58:54,932 --> 00:58:56,048
I am not selling .

665
00:58:56,116 --> 00:58:57,916
But you will get your money when the war 's over .

666
00:58:57,984 --> 00:59:00,970
You don 't appear to understand . I am not selling .

667
00:59:01,038 --> 00:59:02,989
Oh , but you are selling , friend .

668
00:59:03,056 --> 00:59:04,907
And we 'll take that one , there , too .

669
00:59:04,974 --> 00:59:07,827
So you filthy soldier scan butcher my mare ?

670
00:59:07,895 --> 00:59:11,030
Sergeant , he thinks we 're filthy soldiers . Do you hear ?

671
00:59:11,032 --> 00:59:12,164
Aye , I heard .

672
00:59:12,232 --> 00:59:13,949
You can 't go saying things like that , friend .

673
00:59:13,951 --> 00:59:16,919
What he needs is a little army discipline .

674
00:59:16,987 --> 00:59:19,722
I hear you need more pikemen in your platoon , Sergeant .

675
00:59:19,790 --> 00:59:21,356
You 'll pay for this !

676
00:59:22,125 --> 00:59:23,626
( HORSE WHINNYING )

677
00:59:52,222 --> 00:59:54,457
Good horse you had , there . Cost a pretty penny , I reckon .

678
00:59:54,524 --> 00:59:55,824
We robbed the canteen mint .

679
00:59:55,892 --> 00:59:57,293
A right jester , he is .

680
00:59:57,361 --> 00:59:58,794
Yeah , well , a day 's fighting in Cromwell 's army

681
00:59:58,862 --> 01:00:00,262
will soon cure your wit , my lad .

682
01:00:00,330 --> 01:00:01,797
I am not doing any fighting ,

683
01:00:01,865 --> 01:00:04,600
neither for the King or your precious Cromwell , either .

684
01:00:04,667 --> 01:00:06,002
You mark that well , soldier .

685
01:00:06,069 --> 01:00:07,370
Yeah , you coward .

686
01:00:07,437 --> 01:00:08,737
Just like your friend .

687
01:00:08,805 --> 01:00:11,140
- Matthew Hopkins is no friend of mine . - Hopkins ?

688
01:00:11,208 --> 01:00:13,742
The fancy boy who just made a fool of your cavalry , comrade .

689
01:00:13,810 --> 01:00:15,611
- You rode with him . - I had reasons .

690
01:00:15,678 --> 01:00:17,396
- He pays you ? - We were partners .

691
01:00:17,464 --> 01:00:19,398
- In what business ? - Extermination .

692
01:00:19,466 --> 01:00:21,400
- Eh ? - And what does that mean ?

693
01:00:23,153 --> 01:00:24,419
( SCREAMS )

694
01:00:34,014 --> 01:00:35,381
( GUN FIRES )

695
01:00:38,785 --> 01:00:40,086
( PANTING )

696
01:00:56,903 --> 01:00:58,103
( SCREAMS )

697
01:01:51,041 --> 01:01:52,041
( SCREAMS )

698
01:01:59,132 --> 01:02:00,866
( STEARNE SCREAMING )

699
01:03:04,698 --> 01:03:05,831
Now ,

700
01:03:07,233 --> 01:03:11,169
Matthew Hopkins , sir .

701
01:03:20,964 --> 01:03:23,065
Adequate , very adequate .

702
01:03:23,132 --> 01:03:24,399
We did our best , sir .

703
01:03:24,467 --> 01:03:27,002
Lavenham has served me well , Master Webb .

704
01:03:27,070 --> 01:03:29,304
Now I must find out how I can serve you .

705
01:03:29,371 --> 01:03:31,406
They 're all women , sir .

706
01:03:31,474 --> 01:03:33,475
Strange , isn 't it , how much iniquity

707
01:03:33,542 --> 01:03:35,477
the Lord vested in the female ?

708
01:03:35,544 --> 01:03:37,479
Pardon , sir ?

709
01:03:37,546 --> 01:03:39,180
Who makes the accusations ?

710
01:03:39,248 --> 01:03:41,683
Myself , sir . I 'm representing the town .

711
01:03:41,751 --> 01:03:43,551
- How many ? - Three , sir .

712
01:03:43,620 --> 01:03:45,153
And what age ?

713
01:03:45,221 --> 01:03:47,489
Well , two are young , sir , Elizabeth Clark and Mary Reynolds .

714
01:03:47,556 --> 01:03:49,424
The other 's worn and old .

715
01:03:49,492 --> 01:03:51,693
Fetch the young pair here to me .

716
01:03:51,761 --> 01:03:52,861
What of the other hag ?

717
01:03:52,929 --> 01:03:55,363
Well , the old ones are more sensible .

718
01:03:55,431 --> 01:03:57,532
It 's the young ones who are stubborn .

719
01:03:57,600 --> 01:03:58,834
They require time .

720
01:03:58,901 --> 01:04:00,268
Oh , I see .

721
01:04:02,705 --> 01:04:04,022
- Sir ? - Yes , man ?

722
01:04:04,090 --> 01:04:05,323
Your assistant , sir .

723
01:04:05,391 --> 01:04:08,093
We were told he , too , would be coming to Lavenham .

724
01:04:08,161 --> 01:04:09,727
He 's engaged elsewhere .

725
01:04:09,795 --> 01:04:11,863
He 's fighting for the Parliamentary cause .

726
01:04:11,931 --> 01:04:14,999
Oh . He will be joining you here , sir ?

727
01:04:15,068 --> 01:04:16,301
I really can 't say .

728
01:04:16,369 --> 01:04:17,635
You can manage without him ?

729
01:04:17,703 --> 01:04:18,904
Of course .

730
01:04:18,971 --> 01:04:21,323
- I apologize ... - No .

731
01:04:21,390 --> 01:04:22,924
Not only can I manage without him ,

732
01:04:22,991 --> 01:04:25,927
but I intend to instigate a new method of execution ,

733
01:04:25,994 --> 01:04:31,533
and you , Master Webb , you shall aid mein carrying it out .

734
01:04:31,600 --> 01:04:32,834
What 's that , sir ?

735
01:04:32,901 --> 01:04:35,102
You 'll see .

736
01:04:35,170 --> 01:04:39,507
It 's a fitting end for the foul ungodliness in womankind .

737
01:04:39,575 --> 01:04:41,543
Yes , sir .

738
01:04:41,610 --> 01:04:43,345
Now , fetch that young pair here .

739
01:04:43,412 --> 01:04:44,546
Sir .

740
01:04:59,512 --> 01:05:01,712
An excellent meal , gentlemen .

741
01:05:04,300 --> 01:05:06,401
There is little I find so satisfying

742
01:05:06,469 --> 01:05:08,836
as good food after a well-earned victory .

743
01:05:08,904 --> 01:05:10,772
- Wouldn 't you agree ? - Entirely , General .

744
01:05:10,839 --> 01:05:14,058
The conflict at Naseby , sir , will go down as a triumph of your strategy .

745
01:05:14,126 --> 01:05:15,393
Perhaps .

746
01:05:15,461 --> 01:05:17,161
I would rather that it went down

747
01:05:17,229 --> 01:05:19,281
as a triumph for the forces of true godliness .

748
01:05:19,348 --> 01:05:22,483
Nevertheless , your name will symbolize the victory , sir .

749
01:05:22,551 --> 01:05:24,569
Whether I like it or not , eh , Captain ?

750
01:05:34,430 --> 01:05:38,083
That cornet you so highly recommended to me , is he to join us ?

751
01:05:38,150 --> 01:05:39,484
He 's coming now , General Cromwell .

752
01:05:39,551 --> 01:05:40,851
Good .

753
01:05:40,919 --> 01:05:44,689
Amongst the most pleasurable aspects of victory , gentlemen ,

754
01:05:44,756 --> 01:05:47,858
is the opportunity it affords to reward valor .

755
01:05:47,926 --> 01:05:50,178
It ranks almost with good food .

756
01:05:51,547 --> 01:05:52,580
Cornet Marshall , sir .

757
01:05:52,648 --> 01:05:55,316
Mmm . All right . Rest , Cornet .

758
01:06:00,272 --> 01:06:03,308
Your captain has told me about you .

759
01:06:03,375 --> 01:06:04,942
He says you 're a good soldier .

760
01:06:05,010 --> 01:06:07,178
Thank you , sir .

761
01:06:07,246 --> 01:06:09,714
He recommends that I promote you to captain .

762
01:06:09,781 --> 01:06:11,299
I thank you , sir .

763
01:06:11,366 --> 01:06:14,936
I have a special mission for you , Captain .

764
01:06:15,003 --> 01:06:18,105
Take three men and ride back into East Anglia .

765
01:06:18,173 --> 01:06:19,707
The King has escaped us

766
01:06:19,842 --> 01:06:22,643
and is rumored to be making for the Norfolk coast .

767
01:06:22,711 --> 01:06:25,113
If that is the case , find and apprehend him

768
01:06:25,181 --> 01:06:27,231
before he can escape to the continent .

769
01:06:27,299 --> 01:06:28,332
It 's an honor , sir .

770
01:06:28,400 --> 01:06:30,969
Pick your men . Start at once .

771
01:06:31,037 --> 01:06:35,289
If you find the King , you will escort him then to Norwich .

772
01:06:35,357 --> 01:06:37,492
If not , join us in the west .

773
01:06:37,560 --> 01:06:39,744
Good luck , Captain .

774
01:06:49,705 --> 01:06:52,473
Shall we rest up for the night , Richard ?

775
01:06:52,541 --> 01:06:55,276
We 've got a job to do . We 'll go on till we 've done it .

776
01:06:55,344 --> 01:06:57,445
Do you mean looking for the King ?

777
01:06:57,513 --> 01:06:59,947
Or finding Hopkins and Stearne ?

778
01:07:00,015 --> 01:07:01,783
Both .

779
01:07:01,850 --> 01:07:04,152
Richard , you can 't go off and desert again .

780
01:07:04,220 --> 01:07:05,920
I don 't plan to desert !

781
01:07:05,988 --> 01:07:08,790
But supposing you do find out where they are ?

782
01:07:08,857 --> 01:07:10,458
Then I shall take temporary leave again .

783
01:07:10,526 --> 01:07:13,077
For God 's sake , Richard , I know how you feel ,

784
01:07:13,145 --> 01:07:17,115
but to risk court-martial to kill Parliament 's own appointees ,

785
01:07:17,182 --> 01:07:18,616
you 'll be hanged yourself .

786
01:07:18,684 --> 01:07:22,920
Robert ! I 've taken an oath . I won 't break it !

787
01:07:22,988 --> 01:07:24,205
It 's madness !

788
01:07:24,273 --> 01:07:25,373
It 's justice !

789
01:07:26,708 --> 01:07:28,409
It 's my justice .

790
01:07:32,748 --> 01:07:34,382
HORSE SELLER : And what about one of them , sir ?

791
01:07:34,450 --> 01:07:36,684
You won 't find better horseflesh in the whole of Suffolk .

792
01:07:36,752 --> 01:07:40,638
So , how much you going to try to drag out of me if I take that one ?

793
01:07:40,706 --> 01:07:42,306
He 's yours for a couple of guineas , sir .

794
01:07:42,374 --> 01:07:43,508
A guinea .

795
01:07:43,576 --> 01:07:44,976
A guinea and a half

796
01:07:45,043 --> 01:07:46,243
for getting me out of bed at this hour of the morning .

797
01:07:46,311 --> 01:07:47,411
One guinea .

798
01:07:47,480 --> 01:07:48,546
And a quarter ?

799
01:07:48,614 --> 01:07:50,014
I 'll quarter you .

800
01:07:50,082 --> 01:07:51,616
You drive a hard bargain , sir .

801
01:07:51,684 --> 01:07:52,851
Yeah .

802
01:07:52,918 --> 01:07:54,352
And where would you be heading

803
01:07:54,419 --> 01:07:55,820
that you need a horse in such a hurry ?

804
01:07:55,888 --> 01:07:58,389
- To find my partner . - Your partner , eh ?

805
01:07:58,457 --> 01:08:00,725
And what line of business might you be in ?

806
01:08:00,793 --> 01:08:02,794
God 's business , witch-finding .

807
01:08:02,862 --> 01:08:04,929
Witch-finding . Oh , that 's nice .

808
01:08:04,997 --> 01:08:06,430
That 's very nice .

809
01:08:06,499 --> 01:08:10,167
You wouldn 't make it a guinea and a quarter , would you ?

810
01:08:10,235 --> 01:08:13,004
Do you know a man called Matthew Hopkins ?

811
01:08:13,939 --> 01:08:15,006
You know where he is ?

812
01:08:15,073 --> 01:08:17,575
I heard tell of such a man down south .

813
01:08:17,643 --> 01:08:18,877
Lavenham , I believe .

814
01:08:18,944 --> 01:08:20,812
What 's he doing in Lavenham ?

815
01:08:20,880 --> 01:08:23,280
Extracting confessions , I don 't doubt .

816
01:08:23,348 --> 01:08:26,317
You let me have that four-legged cripple now !

817
01:08:43,352 --> 01:08:46,354
This happened three days ago . Why didn 't you report it to the militia then ?

818
01:08:46,422 --> 01:08:48,489
How should we know it was the King himself ?

819
01:08:48,557 --> 01:08:50,191
A stranger , obviously a townsman ,

820
01:08:50,259 --> 01:08:52,160
tries to hire a boat to cross to France

821
01:08:52,227 --> 01:08:53,428
and you suspect nothing ?

822
01:08:53,496 --> 01:08:55,179
When the country 's torn by civil war ?

823
01:08:55,247 --> 01:08:56,581
I didn 't know there was a war on

824
01:08:56,649 --> 01:08:58,265
till you gentlemen told me so .

825
01:08:58,333 --> 01:08:59,968
Oh , come on , Richard . We 'd better go back .

826
01:09:00,035 --> 01:09:02,887
Aye , I suppose so . I want to pass through Lavenham and see how Sara is .

827
01:09:02,955 --> 01:09:05,423
- Lavenham ? - Aye , how far is it from here ?

828
01:09:05,491 --> 01:09:06,974
About two days ride , I reckon .

829
01:09:07,042 --> 01:09:08,643
They got more excitement over there

830
01:09:08,710 --> 01:09:10,311
than any of your city folk 's wars .

831
01:09:10,378 --> 01:09:13,264
- What do you mean ? - They 're burning witches there , I hear .

832
01:09:13,332 --> 01:09:14,532
Some such rigmarole .

833
01:09:14,600 --> 01:09:16,184
They 're in Lavenham !

834
01:09:16,252 --> 01:09:17,402
( RICHARD URGING HORSE )

835
01:09:17,470 --> 01:09:19,103
Oy ! Richard !

836
01:09:55,975 --> 01:09:56,775
( SCREAMING )

837
01:09:59,344 --> 01:10:02,730
Elizabeth ! Elizabeth !

838
01:10:03,466 --> 01:10:05,200
Oh , God !

839
01:10:07,319 --> 01:10:08,986
All is ready , Master Hopkins ?

840
01:10:09,054 --> 01:10:10,521
Aye .

841
01:10:10,589 --> 01:10:12,973
Proceed with the executions , then .

842
01:10:16,728 --> 01:10:18,513
Bring forth Elizabeth Clark .

843
01:10:18,581 --> 01:10:21,599
( WOMAN SCREAMING ) Right . Siegel , fetch the rope .

844
01:10:28,974 --> 01:10:30,474
MAN 1 : Get the rope .

845
01:10:30,542 --> 01:10:31,593
MAN 2 : Oh , come on , you little bitch !

846
01:10:43,823 --> 01:10:44,939
No ! Help !

847
01:10:46,041 --> 01:10:47,174
No !

848
01:10:55,751 --> 01:10:58,485
( SCREAMING )

849
01:11:31,737 --> 01:11:32,770
No !

850
01:12:04,436 --> 01:12:05,853
Lower away .

851
01:12:05,920 --> 01:12:07,321
Slowly , now . Keep her slow .

852
01:12:32,865 --> 01:12:34,832
Elizabeth !

853
01:12:50,315 --> 01:12:52,399
Master Hopkins , there are two more to be burned .

854
01:12:52,467 --> 01:12:56,320
Yes , Magistrate . Master Webb , the others !

855
01:13:26,685 --> 01:13:28,469
Here you are , 12 guineas in silver .

856
01:13:28,537 --> 01:13:31,105
To be spent in the service of our Lord , Magistrate .

857
01:13:31,172 --> 01:13:33,574
We must thank you for your good work , Master Witchfinder .

858
01:13:33,642 --> 01:13:36,176
Thank you , Magistrate , for your aid .

859
01:13:45,237 --> 01:13:46,737
Witchfinder !

860
01:13:46,788 --> 01:13:47,755
Greetings , Stearne .

861
01:13:47,822 --> 01:13:49,123
Is that all you 've got to say

862
01:13:49,190 --> 01:13:50,625
after leaving me therewith Cromwell 's men ?

863
01:13:50,693 --> 01:13:53,127
Well , I provided us both with the opportunity to escape .

864
01:13:53,195 --> 01:13:54,979
Only you did and I was captured .

865
01:13:55,046 --> 01:13:58,116
Fortunes of war , Stearne .

866
01:13:58,183 --> 01:14:02,403
You know me well enough to know that I wouldn 't hesitate to fire and kill you .

867
01:14:02,470 --> 01:14:04,171
Aye , you would that .

868
01:14:04,239 --> 01:14:08,742
I hold all human life dearly , Stearne , especially my own .

869
01:14:08,810 --> 01:14:10,144
Oh , come now .

870
01:14:10,212 --> 01:14:12,213
You 've escaped and all is well .

871
01:14:12,848 --> 01:14:13,848
Maybe .

872
01:14:13,916 --> 01:14:16,116
I even saved your share of the pay

873
01:14:16,184 --> 01:14:18,319
even though I did all of the work myself .

874
01:14:18,386 --> 01:14:21,556
Now , are you going to be sensible or do I kill you ?

875
01:14:24,092 --> 01:14:25,809
By the way , do you know what they call me now ?

876
01:14:25,878 --> 01:14:27,178
What ?

877
01:14:27,246 --> 01:14:29,180
Witchfinder General .

878
01:14:29,248 --> 01:14:30,614
There are those who think

879
01:14:30,682 --> 01:14:33,017
that I should be appointed such for all of England ,

880
01:14:33,085 --> 01:14:35,052
appointed by Parliament .

881
01:14:36,188 --> 01:14:37,621
Here ! Look .

882
01:14:39,925 --> 01:14:40,908
Sara . She 's here .

883
01:14:40,976 --> 01:14:42,193
Very nice , eh , Matthew ?

884
01:14:42,261 --> 01:14:43,277
No , you fool .

885
01:14:43,345 --> 01:14:45,312
Don 't you realize that if she 's here ,

886
01:14:45,380 --> 01:14:47,314
that trooper must be around , too ?

887
01:14:47,382 --> 01:14:48,850
But he 's away fighting .

888
01:14:48,917 --> 01:14:51,418
Suppose he got leave after Naseby .

889
01:14:51,487 --> 01:14:53,554
Where do you think he 'd go ? To see her , of course .

890
01:14:53,622 --> 01:14:55,089
We better move along then , eh ? No .

891
01:14:55,156 --> 01:14:57,691
That man , Marshall , is not going to give up .

892
01:14:57,759 --> 01:14:59,793
He 's proved that to us already .

893
01:14:59,861 --> 01:15:01,412
Then we have to get him before he gets us , right ?

894
01:15:01,479 --> 01:15:04,098
We have the power to do it , legally .

895
01:15:04,166 --> 01:15:05,332
Prove him a witch , huh ?

896
01:15:05,400 --> 01:15:06,884
Exactly .

897
01:15:06,952 --> 01:15:08,136
He 'd never confess , not that one .

898
01:15:08,203 --> 01:15:10,488
On his own , no .

899
01:15:10,556 --> 01:15:13,123
But if we had him and the girl ?

900
01:15:13,125 --> 01:15:15,809
Yeah , she 's the niece of a man we executed for witchcraft .

901
01:15:15,877 --> 01:15:17,745
And Marshall is her husband .

902
01:15:17,813 --> 01:15:19,580
I owe that jumped-up plowboy a seeing-to .

903
01:15:19,647 --> 01:15:21,248
Go out and ask around .

904
01:15:21,316 --> 01:15:23,484
Find out if he 's been seen .

905
01:15:23,486 --> 01:15:27,689
If not , we 'll tarry here a while until he does arrive .

906
01:15:40,903 --> 01:15:43,237
( KNOCK ON DOOR )

907
01:15:43,305 --> 01:15:46,223
- Who is it ? - RICHARD : Sara , open the door . It 's me .

908
01:15:48,126 --> 01:15:49,459
Richard ?

909
01:16:04,143 --> 01:16:05,409
They were here , Hopkins and Stearne .

910
01:16:05,477 --> 01:16:06,744
I didn 't know what to do . I saw them in the street .

911
01:16:06,812 --> 01:16:07,945
- I didn 't know if they saw me or not . - I know .

912
01:16:08,013 --> 01:16:09,380
I know .

913
01:16:14,619 --> 01:16:18,088
Well , I 'll be in the tavern with the others , then .

914
01:16:35,907 --> 01:16:37,658
He 's here , Matthew ! Just arrived .

915
01:16:37,726 --> 01:16:39,226
- Where 's he gone ? - To see the girl .

916
01:16:39,294 --> 01:16:41,311
- Alone ? - Yeah . The three others are in the tavern .

917
01:16:41,379 --> 01:16:43,480
Go and get us an extra man to help .

918
01:16:43,548 --> 01:16:44,731
Where are we going to take them , Matthew ?

919
01:16:44,799 --> 01:16:46,250
Up to the castle .

920
01:16:46,318 --> 01:16:48,686
The magistrate here is very helpful .

921
01:16:48,753 --> 01:16:50,388
That 's where you interrogated the others , is it ?

922
01:16:50,390 --> 01:16:52,190
Yes .

923
01:16:52,257 --> 01:16:54,257
Now , hurry to it , man .

924
01:17:16,865 --> 01:17:19,333
What are you going to do ?

925
01:17:19,401 --> 01:17:22,169
You say Hopkins arrived two days ago .

926
01:17:22,237 --> 01:17:25,740
Yes , and then he was with the other one in the street today .

927
01:17:26,608 --> 01:17:27,941
And they haven 't left yet ?

928
01:17:28,009 --> 01:17:30,711
I 'm not sure . I 've been too scared to leave .

929
01:17:30,779 --> 01:17:32,946
HOPKINS : Come on ! Open up in there !

930
01:17:33,014 --> 01:17:34,448
( KNOCKING ON DOOR )

931
01:17:46,778 --> 01:17:48,929
Drop that sword , soldier .

932
01:17:55,787 --> 01:17:59,540
This man accuses you , Sara Lowes , and you , Richard Marshall ,

933
01:17:59,608 --> 01:18:00,875
of consorting with the Devil .

934
01:18:00,943 --> 01:18:02,843
- Is that not so , Master Webb ? - It is that , sir .

935
01:18:02,911 --> 01:18:04,946
Will you describe your evidence to us ?

936
01:18:04,980 --> 01:18:07,497
I observed the accused talking with their familiars

937
01:18:07,565 --> 01:18:09,216
and making the signs of Satan , sir .

938
01:18:09,283 --> 01:18:11,986
And what were these familiars to which you refer ?

939
01:18:12,053 --> 01:18:13,804
Black cat and a stoat , sir .

940
01:18:13,872 --> 01:18:16,774
You 're a very observing citizen , Master Webb .

941
01:18:17,676 --> 01:18:20,561
Well , Sara , do you confess ?

942
01:18:23,798 --> 01:18:26,416
And what do you have to say , soldier ?

943
01:18:29,271 --> 01:18:32,172
I 'm going to kill you , Hopkins .

944
01:18:32,240 --> 01:18:34,308
I don 't think you 'll find that easy .

945
01:18:34,376 --> 01:18:36,611
The law is with me , remember ?

946
01:18:36,678 --> 01:18:40,131
And what are you ? An accused witch .

947
01:18:40,198 --> 01:18:41,616
They must be submitted to the test .

948
01:18:41,683 --> 01:18:42,850
Take them , Stearne .

949
01:18:52,394 --> 01:18:53,694
Hopkins !

950
01:18:55,597 --> 01:18:56,497
( SCREAMING )

951
01:18:58,650 --> 01:19:00,718
HOPKINS : A Royalist sympathizer , evidently .

952
01:19:00,785 --> 01:19:02,136
But what are we going to do with him ?

953
01:19:02,204 --> 01:19:04,971
Leave him . I 'll inform the magistrate later .

954
01:19:05,039 --> 01:19:07,625
We have more important work to do .

955
01:19:07,692 --> 01:19:09,159
Come on .

956
01:19:11,129 --> 01:19:12,863
Get moving .

957
01:19:35,019 --> 01:19:37,488
Orders from the magistrate . Suspected witches .

958
01:19:37,556 --> 01:19:39,323
Yes , sir . Sorry , sir .

959
01:20:20,865 --> 01:20:22,866
I heard them .

960
01:20:22,934 --> 01:20:24,535
ROBERT : Where are they taking them ?

961
01:20:25,770 --> 01:20:28,272
To the castle to test them .

962
01:20:28,339 --> 01:20:29,673
Test them ?

963
01:20:30,675 --> 01:20:35,245
They 're accused of witchcraft .

964
01:20:35,313 --> 01:20:36,780
- Harcourt , you come with me . - Yes , sir .

965
01:20:36,847 --> 01:20:37,881
Shall I look after him , sir ?

966
01:20:37,949 --> 01:20:39,749
Yes , try and find him a physician .

967
01:20:39,817 --> 01:20:42,852
I 've heard much of how Hopkins conducts his interrogations .

968
01:20:42,920 --> 01:20:44,621
Come on , Harcourt .

969
01:20:46,324 --> 01:20:47,324
( COUGHS )

970
01:21:02,123 --> 01:21:03,774
All right , Stearne .

971
01:21:09,013 --> 01:21:09,763
( SARA AND RICHARD SCREAMING )

972
01:21:15,203 --> 01:21:16,704
( SARA WHIMPERING )

973
01:21:20,475 --> 01:21:22,175
( SCREAMING )

974
01:21:25,764 --> 01:21:27,715
SARA : No !

975
01:21:34,038 --> 01:21:37,007
Well , Captain Marshall , do you now confess ?

976
01:21:40,078 --> 01:21:43,046
Keep at it , Stearne . You 're doing God 's work .

977
01:21:44,649 --> 01:21:46,433
( SARA SCREAMING )

978
01:21:56,627 --> 01:21:58,278
Put her over here .

979
01:21:58,346 --> 01:21:59,947
And you , Master Webb , help him .

980
01:22:20,334 --> 01:22:22,469
Master Hopkins and his assistants , are they here , man ?

981
01:22:22,537 --> 01:22:24,304
- That they are , sir . - Well , let us pass , then .

982
01:22:24,372 --> 01:22:25,972
You 're here to help the Witchfinder ?

983
01:22:26,040 --> 01:22:27,224
We 're here to find him , yes .

984
01:22:27,292 --> 01:22:28,642
Have you a signed pass ?

985
01:22:34,682 --> 01:22:40,570
Sara , I 'm going to place this iron on your back .

986
01:22:40,638 --> 01:22:42,473
Should you faint or cry out ,

987
01:22:42,540 --> 01:22:47,010
we can only take it that Satan has intervened to spare you your agony .

988
01:22:48,396 --> 01:22:50,848
However , I could show mercy if ...

989
01:22:52,817 --> 01:22:56,820
If Captain Marshall were to confess to witchcraft first .

990
01:22:56,888 --> 01:22:58,988
But will you do it , sir ?

991
01:22:59,657 --> 01:23:01,559
I shall kill you .

992
01:23:01,626 --> 01:23:03,277
So , you have no proper authorization , then .

993
01:23:03,345 --> 01:23:04,478
What do you mean ?

994
01:23:04,545 --> 01:23:06,046
From the magistrate . Authorization .

995
01:23:06,114 --> 01:23:07,681
Not here with us , no .

996
01:23:07,748 --> 01:23:09,383
Well , we 'll go back and get one then .

997
01:23:09,451 --> 01:23:11,618
All right . Then I 'll let you pass .

998
01:23:17,242 --> 01:23:19,243
Master Webb , go and see what is the matter .

999
01:23:19,294 --> 01:23:21,095
Yes , Master Hopkins .

1000
01:23:22,397 --> 01:23:23,664
What do we do , Matthew ?

1001
01:23:23,731 --> 01:23:26,333
We shall carry on with God 's work as before , man .

1002
01:23:26,401 --> 01:23:28,335
And fetch Captain Marshall over here .

1003
01:23:28,402 --> 01:23:30,937
He shall kneel before his wife and watch her suffer .

1004
01:23:31,005 --> 01:23:32,405
- But Matthew ... - Go do it , man !

1005
01:23:51,826 --> 01:23:52,893
( SCREAMS )

1006
01:24:20,371 --> 01:24:21,771
Oh , God !

1007
01:24:42,077 --> 01:24:44,111
You took him away from me .

1008
01:24:44,179 --> 01:24:46,146
You took him from me .

1009
01:24:46,214 --> 01:24:48,182
You took him from me .

1010
01:24:48,250 --> 01:24:50,150
You took him from me !

1011
01:24:50,218 --> 01:24:52,586
( YELLING ) You took him from me !

1012
01:24:53,988 --> 01:24:55,405
( SOBBING )

1013
01:25:05,083 --> 01:25:06,984
May God have mercy on us all .

1014
01:25:09,471 --> 01:25:11,938
( SCREAMING HYSTERICALLY )

